WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.158
It rained. Is the whole day ruined?

00:00:03.158 --> 00:00:06.316
Disappointment is real. The conclusion can be examined.

00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:09.474
A 2012 meta-analysis compared regulation strategies.

00:00:09.474 --> 00:00:12.632
Reappraisal concerns changing a situation’s meaning.

00:00:12.632 --> 00:00:15.789
Effects depend on strategy and context.

00:00:15.789 --> 00:00:22.105
The exhibition was cancelled. That happened.

00:00:22.105 --> 00:00:28.421
“Every effort was wasted” goes further.

00:00:28.421 --> 00:00:34.737
The artwork might find another venue.

00:00:34.737 --> 00:00:41.053
Compare interpretations to find possible actions.

00:00:41.053 --> 00:00:44.211
You need not erase disappointment.

00:00:44.211 --> 00:00:47.368
Harm cannot be solved by reframing alone.

00:00:47.368 --> 00:00:50.526
Protection, resources and changed conditions matter.

00:00:50.526 --> 00:00:56.842
Acknowledge the facts and name the feeling.

00:00:56.842 --> 00:01:03.158
Ask one concrete question: what remains possible?

00:01:03.158 --> 00:01:06.316
Feeling no relief does not mean failure.

00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:09.474
Keep the rain real. Explore another route.

00:01:09.474 --> 00:01:12.632
Disappointment and a next step can coexist.

00:01:12.632 --> 00:01:15.789
Leave today an ending still to be written.
